<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>ProvenanceLens report: {{ r.file.name }}</title>
<style>
:root { --bg:#f6f6f3; --panel:#fff; --ink:#1d2025; --muted:#5f6670; --line:#e1e1dc; --accent:#9a3412; --accent-bg:#fff1e6;
  --edited:#b45309; --edited-bg:#fef3c7; --gen:#7c3aed; --gen-bg:#ede9fe; --ok:#15803d; --ok-bg:#dcfce7; --na:#6b7280; --na-bg:#f1f1ef; --code:#f1f1ee; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg:#121315; --panel:#1b1d20; --ink:#e7e7e4; --muted:#9aa0a8; --line:#2d3035; --accent:#fb923c;
  --accent-bg:#3a2214; --edited:#fbbf24; --edited-bg:#3a2d10; --gen:#c4b5fd; --gen-bg:#2a2140; --ok:#4ade80; --ok-bg:#12301f; --na:#9aa0a8; --na-bg:#25272b; --code:#24272b; } }
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink); font:14px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif; }
main { max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:24px 16px 60px; }
h1 { font-size:22px; margin:0 0 2px; } h2 { font-size:16.5px; margin:30px 0 10px; } h3 { font-size:13.5px; margin:14px 0 6px; }
.sub { color:var(--muted); font-size:12.5px; word-break:break-all; }
.hero { display:grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,320px) minmax(0,1fr); gap:20px; margin-top:16px; }
@media (max-width:760px) { .hero { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
.hero img { width:100%; border-radius:10px; border:1px solid var(--line); background:var(--panel); }
.panel { background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px; }
.verdict { display:grid; gap:10px; }
.q { padding:10px 12px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid var(--line); }
.q b { display:block; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:3px; }
.lvl-strong, .lvl-moderate { background:var(--edited-bg); } .lvl-weak { background:var(--na-bg); } .lvl-none { background:var(--ok-bg); }
.gen { background:var(--gen-bg); } .limited { background:var(--na-bg); }
.headline { font-size:15px; font-weight:600; }
.grid2 { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr)); gap:14px; }
.maps { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr)); gap:14px; }
.maps figure { margin:0; } .maps img { width:100%; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid var(--line); }
figcaption { font-size:12.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-top:4px; }
.tablewrap { overflow-x:auto; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; background:var(--panel); }
table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:12.8px; }
th, td { text-align:left; padding:7px 9px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); vertical-align:top; }
th { color:var(--muted); font-size:11.5px; font-weight:600; white-space:nowrap; }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom:0; }
.pill { display:inline-block; padding:1px 8px; border-radius:999px; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:600; white-space:nowrap; }
.s-edited, .s-failure { background:var(--edited-bg); color:var(--edited); } .s-generated { background:var(--gen-bg); color:var(--gen); }
.s-authentic, .s-success { background:var(--ok-bg); color:var(--ok); } .s-neutral, .s-not_applicable, .s-informational, .s-declared { background:var(--na-bg); color:var(--na); }
.bar { height:6px; width:80px; background:var(--code); border-radius:3px; position:relative; margin-top:5px; }
.bar i { position:absolute; left:0; top:0; bottom:0; border-radius:3px; background:var(--accent); }
code, .mono { font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace; font-size:12px; }
.kv { display:grid; grid-template-columns:max-content minmax(0,1fr); gap:3px 14px; font-size:13px; }
.kv div:nth-child(odd) { color:var(--muted); }
.chain { overflow-x:auto; padding:6px 0; }
.qt { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(8,1fr); gap:2px; max-width:260px; }
.qt span { font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace; font-size:10.5px; text-align:center; background:var(--code); border-radius:3px; padding:1px 0; }
details summary { cursor:pointer; color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; }
footer { margin-top:36px; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>ProvenanceLens report</h1>
  <div class="sub">{{ r.file.name }} · {{ r.format }} · {{ "{:,}".format(r.file.size) }} bytes · SHA-256 {{ r.file.sha256 }} · analysed {{ r.generated }} in {{ r.seconds }}s</div>

  <div class="hero">
    <div>{% if r.image and r.image.thumbnail_jpeg_b64 %}<img alt="{{ 'sampled video frames' if r.image.contact_sheet else 'analysed image' }}" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,{{ r.image.thumbnail_jpeg_b64 }}">{% endif %}
      <div class="sub">{% if r.video %}{{ r.video.video }} · {{ r.video.duration_s }} s · {{ r.video.frames_sampled }} frames sampled{% else %}{{ r.image.width }}×{{ r.image.height }} px{% endif %}</div></div>
    <div class="panel verdict">
      <div class="headline">{{ r.verdict.headline }}</div>
      <div class="q {{ 'limited' if r.verdict.limited_signal else '' }}"><b>Where did it come from?</b>{{ r.verdict.provenance }}</div>
      <div class="q lvl-{{ r.verdict.editing_level }}"><b>Has it been changed? — {{ r.verdict.editing_level }} evidence (score {{ "%.2f"|format(r.verdict.editing_score) }})</b>
        {% set top = r.verdict.signals | selectattr('supports', 'equalto', 'edited') | list %}
        {% if top %}{% for s in top[:4] %}{{ s.title }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}No signal above its calibrated threshold.{% endif %}
        {% set decl = r.verdict.signals | selectattr('supports', 'equalto', 'declared') | list %}
        {% if decl %}<div class="sub">Declared by the signer: {{ decl[0].detail }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="q {{ 'gen' if r.verdict.generation_score >= 0.5 else '' }}"><b>AI generation</b>{{ r.verdict.generation }}</div>
      <div class="sub">This is an evidence summary, not a fake/real verdict. Every line below says what was measured and how much it counts; read the signals, not just the headline.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Signals</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>Supports</th><th>Strength × weight</th><th>What was found</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for s in r.verdict.signals %}
      <tr><td><b>{{ s.title }}</b><div class="sub">{{ s.module }} · {{ s.id }}</div></td>
          <td><span class="pill s-{{ s.supports }}">{{ s.supports.replace('_', ' ') }}</span></td>
          <td class="mono">{% if s.supports in ['edited','generated','authentic','declared'] %}{{ "%.2f"|format(s.strength) }} × {{ s.weight }} = {{ "%.2f"|format(s.contribution) }}<div class="bar"><i style="width:{{ (s.contribution*100)|round|int }}%"></i></div>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ s.detail }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="sub" style="margin-top:6px">Scores combine as 1 − ∏(1 − strength × weight) per question. Weights are reliability priors, several measured on a labelled set (see docs/evaluation.md).</div>

  <h2>Content credentials (C2PA)</h2>
  {% set c = r.c2pa %}
  <div class="panel">
    <p style="margin-top:0">{{ c.summary }}</p>
    {% if c.present and c.state != 'error' %}
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="kv">
        <div>Validation state</div><div><b>{{ c.state }}</b></div>
        <div>Trust list</div><div>{% if c.trust_anchors %}{{ c.trust_anchors|join('; ') }}{% else %}<span class="sub">none supplied (pass --trust): a signer can be Valid but never Trusted</span>{% endif %}</div>
        <div>Signer</div><div>{{ c.active.signer.common_name }} <span class="sub">({{ c.active.signer.issuer }})</span></div>
        <div>Signed at</div><div>{{ c.active.signer.time or 'no timestamp' }}</div>
        <div>Algorithm</div><div>{{ c.active.signer.alg }}</div>
        <div>Claim generator</div><div>{{ c.active.claim_generator }}</div>
        <div>Title</div><div>{{ c.active.title }}</div>
        {% if c.hard_binding.checked %}<div>Hard binding (own check)</div><div>{{ 'matches' if c.hard_binding.match else 'DOES NOT MATCH' }} · {{ c.hard_binding.alg }} over all bytes outside {{ c.hard_binding.exclusions|length }} exclusion(s){% if c.hard_binding.exclusion_covers_non_manifest %} — exclusion also covers {{ c.hard_binding.exclusion_covers_non_manifest|join(', ') }}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="margin-top:0">Declared actions</h3>
        {% if c.active.actions %}<ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px">{% for a in c.active.actions %}<li><code>{{ a.action }}</code>{% if a.software %} by {{ a.software }}{% endif %}{% if a.digital_source_type %} · source type <b>{{ a.digital_source_type }}</b>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% else %}<span class="sub">none declared</span>{% endif %}
        {% if c.ai_declared %}<h3>AI declarations</h3><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px">{% for d in c.ai_declared %}<li>{{ d }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% if chain %}<h3>Ingredient graph</h3><div class="chain">{{ chain|safe }}</div>{% endif %}
    {% if c.certificates %}<h3>Signer certificate chain (inspected independently)</h3>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Subject</th><th>Issuer</th><th>Valid</th><th>Key</th><th>EKU</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      {% for cert in c.certificates %}<tr><td>{{ cert.role }}</td><td>{{ cert.subject }}</td><td>{{ cert.issuer }}</td><td class="mono" style="white-space:nowrap">{{ cert.not_before[:10] }} → {{ cert.not_after[:10] }}</td><td>{{ cert.key }}</td><td>{{ cert.eku|join(', ') }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
      </tbody></table></div>
      {% if c.certificate_findings %}<ul>{% for f in c.certificate_findings %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if c.statuses %}<h3>Validation status codes, explained</h3>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>Code</th><th>Scope</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      {% for s in c.statuses %}<tr><td><span class="pill s-{{ s.kind }}">{{ s.kind }}</span></td><td><code>{{ s.code }}</code></td><td>{{ s.scope }}</td><td>{{ s.explain }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
      </tbody></table></div>{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <h2>Metadata</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="panel">
      {% set m = r.metadata.summary %}
      {% if r.metadata.empty %}<p class="sub" style="margin:0">No EXIF, XMP, IPTC or text metadata.</p>{% else %}
      <div class="kv">{% for k, v in m.exif.items() %}<div>{{ k }}</div><div>{{ v }}</div>{% endfor %}
      {% for k, v in m.gps.items() %}<div>{{ k }}</div><div>{{ v }}</div>{% endfor %}
      {% for k, v in m.xmp.items() %}{% if loop.index <= 12 %}<div>{{ k }}</div><div>{{ v }}</div>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% if m.png_text_keys %}<div>PNG text</div><div>{{ m.png_text_keys|join(', ') }}</div>{% endif %}
      {% if m.container %}{% for k, v in m.container.items() %}<div>{{ k }}</div><div>{{ v }}</div>{% endfor %}{% else %}<div>Embedded thumbnail</div><div>{{ m.thumbnail_bytes }} bytes</div>{% endif %}
      <div>Reader</div><div>{{ m.reader }}</div></div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">Consistency rules</h3>
      {% if r.metadata.findings %}<ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px">{% for f in r.metadata.findings %}<li><span class="pill s-{{ 'edited' if f.status in ['edited','inconsistent'] else ('generated' if f.status=='generated' else ('authentic' if f.status=='consistent' else 'neutral')) }}">{{ f.status }}</span> <b>{{ f.title }}</b> — {{ f.detail }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% else %}<p class="sub">No rule fired.</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Compression</h2>
  {% if r.jpeg %}{% set j = r.jpeg %}
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="panel"><div class="kv">
      <div>Encoding</div><div>{{ 'progressive' if j.progressive else 'baseline' }}, {{ j.subsampling }}, {{ j.huffman_tables }} Huffman tables</div>
      <div>Segments</div><div>{{ j.segments|join(' · ') }}</div>
      {% if j.trailing_bytes %}<div>After end-of-image</div><div>{{ j.trailing_bytes }} bytes</div>{% endif %}
      {% if j.qtables %}<div>Closest encoder</div><div><b>{{ j.qtables.best.source }}</b> {{ j.qtables.best.quality }} (distance {{ j.qtables.best.distance }}{% if j.qtables.best.exact %}, exact{% endif %}){% if j.qtables.best.shared_with %}<div class="sub">identical tables also written by: {{ j.qtables.best.shared_with|join('; ') }}</div>{% endif %}</div>
      <div>IJG quality estimate</div><div>{{ j.qtables.ijg_quality_estimate }}{% if j.qtables.ijg_exact %} (exact IJG tables){% endif %}</div>
      <div>Other candidates</div><div>{% for cnd in j.qtables.candidates[1:] %}{{ cnd.source }} {{ cnd.quality }} ({{ cnd.distance }}){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
      <div>Double compression</div><div>{% if j.djpeg.applicable %}<b>{{ 'likely' if j.djpeg.double else 'not detected' }}</b> (score {{ j.djpeg.probability }}, flagged at ≥ {{ j.djpeg.threshold }}) — {{ j.djpeg.note }}{% else %}not applicable: {{ j.djpeg.note }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div></div>
    <div class="panel"><h3 style="margin-top:0">Luminance quantisation table</h3>
      {% if j.luma_table %}<div class="qt">{% for v in j.luma_table %}<span>{{ v }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
      <div class="sub" style="margin-top:6px">Natural (row-major) order. Shared tables identify an encoder library, not an app.</div></div>
  </div>
  {% elif r.video %}<div class="panel"><p class="sub" style="margin:0">{{ r.format }}: video frames carry no JPEG tables and the pixel thresholds were never calibrated on video, so compression and pixel forensics are <b>not applicable</b> (not a pass). The frames above are for the analyst.</p></div>
  {% else %}<div class="panel"><p class="sub" style="margin:0">{{ r.format }}: no JPEG quantisation tables, so encoder fingerprinting and the double-compression test are <b>not applicable</b> (not a pass).</p></div>{% endif %}

  {% if r.pixel %}
  <h2>Pixel maps — pointers for the analyst, not proof</h2>
  <div class="maps">
    {% for name, label, help in [('ela','Error level (ELA)','bright = changes more when re-saved; edges and text are bright too'), ('noise','Noise level','local sensor-noise strength from the finest wavelet band'), ('ghost','JPEG ghost','bright = region differs least when re-saved at the ghost quality')] %}
    {% set mp = r.pixel[name] %}
    <figure><img alt="{{ label }} map" src="data:image/png;base64,{{ mp.heatmap_png_b64 }}">
      <figcaption><b>{{ label }}</b> — {{ help }}. {{ mp.note }}.{% if mp.regions %} Strongest region {{ mp.regions[0].bbox }} (z {{ mp.regions[0].mean_z }}).{% endif %}</figcaption></figure>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Method and limits</h2>
  <div class="panel"><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px">
    <li>A missing C2PA manifest is not evidence of fakery: most genuine images have none.</li>
    <li>ELA lights up on edges, text and saturated areas. It points an analyst at regions; it never decides anything alone.</li>
    <li>The double-compression test sees a second save at <i>higher</i> quality reliably and is nearly blind to a second save at <i>lower</i> quality (the usual platform re-upload).</li>
    <li>No machine-learning "AI detector" is used: AI generation is reported only when it is declared (C2PA, IPTC, embedded generator parameters).</li>
    <li>Metadata is easy to forge; contradictions are informative, a clean result is not.</li>
  </ul></div>
  <footer>ProvenanceLens {{ r.version }} · file SHA-256 {{ r.file.sha256 }}</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
